# sememe program: the ontology (concepts, roles, meaning features).

/// Anything at all: the top of the type hierarchy.
c0 concept Thing < Thing  @0 seed
/// A participant in a conversation, introduced by a speaker tag or as the narrator of written text.
c1 concept Speaker < Thing  @0 seed
/// Something that happens.
c2 concept Event < Thing  @1
/// Something that holds over time.
c3 concept State < Thing  @1
/// A quality of a thing.
c4 concept Property < Thing  @1
/// Interjections, discourse markers and speech acts.
c5 concept Discourse < Thing  @1
/// A living being.
c6 concept Animate < Thing  @1
/// A human being.
c7 concept Person < Animate  @1
/// A non-human animal.
c8 concept Animal < Animate  @1
/// A physical, countable thing.
c9 concept Object < Thing  @1
/// A location.
c10 concept Place < Thing  @1
/// A mass material.
c11 concept Substance < Thing  @1
/// A time or period.
c12 concept Time < Thing  @1
/// An amount or number.
c13 concept Quantity < Thing  @1
/// A cardinal number.
c14 concept Number < Quantity  @1
/// A position in a sequence.
c15 concept Ordinal < Quantity  @1
/// How much of a property.
c16 concept Degree < Property  @1
/// An idea or abstract entity.
c17 concept Abstract < Thing  @1
/// A linking of parts.
c18 concept Coordination < Thing  @1
/// Conjunction: and.
c19 concept And < Coordination  @1
/// Contrast: but.
c20 concept But < Coordination  @1
/// Sense something.
c21 concept Perceive < Event  @1
/// Perceive with the eyes.
c22 concept See < Perceive  @1
/// Convey information.
c23 concept Communicate < Event  @1
/// Utter words.
c24 concept Say < Communicate  @1
/// Say suddenly and with feeling.
c25 concept Exclaim < Say  @1
/// Communicate something to someone.
c26 concept Tell < Communicate  @1
/// Ask someone to do something.
c27 concept Request < Communicate  @1
/// Go on and on talking, nagging or grumbling.
c28 concept Complain < Communicate  @1
/// Converse.
c29 concept Talk < Communicate  @1
/// Talk back, answer.
c30 concept Reply < Communicate  @1
/// Change of position.
c31 concept Move < Event  @1
/// Move away from the deictic center.
c32 concept Go < Move  @1
/// Move toward the deictic center.
c33 concept Come < Move  @1
/// Go away from a place or person.
c34 concept Leave < Move  @1
/// Move on foot.
c35 concept Walk < Move  @1
/// Move house or home.
c36 concept Relocate < Move  @1
/// Move hurriedly with short steps.
c37 concept Scurry < Move  @1
/// Move confusedly and hurriedly.
c38 concept Scuffle < Move  @1
/// Move suddenly and quickly.
c39 concept Dart < Move  @1
/// Move in an arc.
c40 concept Swing < Move  @1
/// Move hastily and awkwardly.
c41 concept Scramble < Move  @1
/// Lower or let fall.
c42 concept Drop < Move  @1
/// Remain in a place.
c43 concept Stay < Event  @1
/// Progress in rank or career.
c44 concept Advance < Event  @1
/// Go out romantically with someone.
c45 concept Date < Event  @1
/// Mental activity.
c46 concept Cognition < Event  @1
/// Believe or consider.
c47 concept Think < Cognition  @1
/// Judge something to be so.
c48 concept Find < Think  @1
/// Have knowledge.
c49 concept Know < Cognition  @1
/// A hypothetical condition (standalone if-clause).
c50 concept Suppose < Cognition  @1
/// Wanting or needing.
c51 concept Desire < Event  @1
/// Wish to have or do.
c52 concept Want < Desire  @1
/// Require.
c53 concept Need < Desire  @1
/// Want rather than something else.
c54 concept Prefer < Want  @1
/// Find pleasant.
c55 concept Like < Event  @1
/// Perform an action.
c56 concept Do < Event  @1
/// Bring into being.
c57 concept Create < Event  @1
/// Produce, prepare.
c58 concept Make < Create  @1
/// Bring about a state or event.
c59 concept Cause < Event  @1
/// Bring back to a former place or state.
c60 concept Restore < Cause  @1
/// Wear someone out.
c61 concept Exhaust < Cause  @1
